General setup:

To get an up-to-date source, do

    setenv CVSROOT /soft/cvs
    cd
    cvs co degas2

This will put the sources in ~/degas2.  (It's not essential that the
sources be in this location.  But this is what the Makefile assumes)

src/.emacs contains a couple of items to consider putting in ~/.emacs.

To get woven documentation:

    mkdir ~/degas2/tex
    cd ~/degas2/tex
    cp ../src/Makefile .
    gmake geometry.print

To compile the code on a Sun:

    mkdir ~/degas2/SUN
    cd ~/degas2/SUN
    cp ../src/Makefile .
    gmake randomtest

To compile the code for the Crays (or HP):

    (On Sun)
    mkdir <some-afs-directory>/degas2/CRAY
    ln -s <same-afs-directory>/degas2/CRAY ~/degas2/CRAY
    cd ~/src/CRAY
    cp ~/degas2/src/Makefile .
    gmake randomtest

    (On Cray)
    ln -s <same-afs-directory>/degas2 ~/degas2
    cd <some-work-directory>/CRAY
    cp ~/degas2/CRAY/Makefile .
    gmake randomtest

To compile the code for CCF:

    (On Sun)
    mkdir ~/degas2/SGI
    cd ~/degas2/SGI
    cp ../src/Makefile .
    gmake randomtest

    (On CCF)
    ln -s /n/lyman/u/<username>/degas2 ~/degas2
    cd ~/degas2/SGI
    gmake randomtest



Description of the programs

etags: a local version of the program to produce tags.

sysdeptest: a test of the various system dependent routines.

reactionwrite: converts cross-section data to REACTION.nc

datasetup: converts elements.input to elements.nc
	converts species.input to species.nc
	converts reactions.input to reactions.nc

problemsetup: converts problem.input and reaction data files to problem.nc

reactionwrite: converts some old Degas input files to netcdf format (to be
superceded by ratecalc).

readgeometry: reads a geometry specification file (specified as arg) to
creates geometry.nc

readbackground: reads background plasma data from degas input file (specified as arg) to
creates background.nc

flighttest: runs flights through the plasma (arg is the number of flights)
-- the prototype for degas 2.

randomtest: a simple test of the random number generator.  A good thing to
try on new architechures.

degasgeom: read a degas input file (as arg) and write out geometry.nc.

geomtesta: a program to plot slices through the geometry.  Reads a file
geometry.inp to determine the slice to plot.  Creates an HDF file
geomtesta.hdf.

readgeometry: read in a text file to specify the geometry.
